; The two rooms of the farmhouse ground floor, in the model's own coordinates.
; The boundary of these boxes IS the threshold -- the front face of MainRoom
; sits in the doorway at z = -0.16, which is the inside face of the front wall,
; so the reveal fires as the player steps through the door and not while they
; are still on the porch.
;
; Two shapes on one Area3D rather than one box, because the ground floor is an
; L: a single box big enough to hold the wing would also stick out through the
; front wall and put half the porch inside the house. Area3D reports entering
; once for the whole area however many shapes it is made of, so walking from
; the main room into the wing is not a crossing -- which it must not be, or the
; roof would slam back on every time the player went to the workbench.
;
; Wing overlaps MainRoom by 0.44 m through the divider doorway. Abutting exactly
; would leave one frame, at some frame rate, where the capsule is inside neither.
[sub_resource type="BoxShape3D" id="BoxShape3D_room_main"]
size = Vector3(6.88, 3.2, 5.68)

[sub_resource type="BoxShape3D" id="BoxShape3D_room_wing"]
size = Vector3(3.28, 3.2, 4.04)

; Where the player can reach the front door: the porch in front of it, plus the
; doorway itself. The door leaf spans x 1.30 .. 2.30 at z 0 and the steps come
; up at x 1.35 .. 2.25, so this covers the whole approach a player who walked
; up the steps is standing on.
[sub_resource type="BoxShape3D" id="BoxShape3D_doorstep"]
size = Vector3(2.4, 3.2, 2.6)

[node name="Main" type="Node3D" unique_id=1508188971]

