; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The snow in the air. Style document sections 21-23.
;
; TWO INSTANCES AND NOT ONE, and the split is the point rather than an
; oversight. scenes/effects/snowfall.tscn holds the director and the two layers
; that fall in WORLD space; it can sit anywhere, because the director places
; both of them over whatever the camera is looking at, every frame.
;
; SnowLens is the third layer and belongs to the CAMERA -- it is the flake that
; crosses the picture, and style document section 23 is explicit that it does
; not need to be in world space. It finds the director on its own, through the
; group SnowfallLayer publishes itself in, so nothing here wires the two
; together and neither node holds a reference to the other.
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

[node name="Snowfall" parent="." instance=ExtResource("27_snowfall")]

[node name="SnowLens" parent="CameraRig/Camera3D" instance=ExtResource("28_snow_lens")]
